# Git
#
# `.git` is intentionally NOT excluded. `crates/glaucus/build.rs` runs `git
# rev-parse --short=12 HEAD` (and `git status --porcelain` for the `-dirty`
# suffix) to stamp `GIT_COMMIT` into every binary's `--version` output; it
# degrades to `unknown` rather than failing when `.git` is absent, so nothing
# would have warned that provenance had gone silently useless in exactly the
# artefact where it matters most. `build.rs` has no environment-variable
# override for this (unlike `RUSTC_VERSION`), and it lives under `crates/`,
# out of this task's scope to add one to -- so excluding `.git` from the build
# context was the only way this ever broke, and un-excluding it is the fix.
# The repo's `.git` is ~14 MB, not the multi-GB `target/` this file exists to
# keep out, so the context-size cost is negligible.
#
# Trade-off worth knowing: `docs/`, `scripts/` and non-README `*.md` stay
# excluded below for their own (much larger) size reasons, but they ARE
# git-tracked. With `.git` present and those paths absent, `git status
# --porcelain` sees them as locally deleted, so every image -- even from a
# clean tagged release -- reports `<hash>-dirty` rather than a bare hash.
# `-dirty` therefore stops meaning "uncommitted changes" and starts meaning
# "built inside a Dockerfile whose context trims non-code paths" -- still far
# better than the previous `unknown`, but not literally accurate. Fixing that
# fully would mean either shipping `docs/`/`scripts/` in every build context
# (defeats the purpose of excluding a 300+ MB docs site) or teaching
# `build.rs` to scope `git status` to build-relevant paths, which is out of
# this task's scope (`crates/` is off-limits here). Documented instead of
# silently accepted.
.gitignore

# IDE
.idea
.vscode
*.iml

# Build artifacts
target/
*.log

# Documentation
*.md
!README.md
docs/
ROAD_MAP.md
CONFIGURATION.md
DOCKER.md
QUICKSTART.md
LOCALSTACK.md

# Config examples (we'll mount these)
config/

# LocalStack
backend/continuous-development/localstack-init/
docker-compose.yml

# Scripts
scripts/

# Environment
.env
.env.*

# Test files
tests/
*.test
